export const SAFETY_STRINGS = {
  'Road or scooter accident': '公路或摩托车事故',
  'By far the most likely serious emergency a traveller faces in this region.': '这是旅行者在本地区面临的、迄今最可能发生的严重紧急情况。',
  'Get out of the traffic lane before anything else. Being hit a second time is a real risk on a fast road, and it is what turns a survivable crash into a fatal one.': '首先离开车道。在快速道路上被二次撞击是真实的风险，而这正是把本来可以挺过去的事故变成致命事故的原因。',
  'Call the national emergency number. Say the road, the direction of travel and the nearest landmark or kilometre marker — a screenshot of your map pin is the fastest way to answer "where are you?".': '请拨打全国紧急电话。说明道路、行驶方向以及最近的地标或公里标，用地图标记的截图回答“您在哪里？”最快。',
  'Do not move anyone who has hit their head or complains of neck or back pain, unless leaving them is more dangerous than moving them.': '对头部受过撞击或主诉颈部、背部疼痛的人，请不要移动，除非留在原地比移动更危险。',
  'Control heavy bleeding with firm, continuous pressure through whatever cloth you have. Keep pressing; do not lift to check.': '用您手头任何布料持续用力按压，以控制大出血。请一直按压，不要抬起来查看。',
  'Go to hospital even if you feel fine. Head injuries and internal bleeding declare themselves hours later, and road rash here infects fast in the heat.': '即使您觉得没事，也要去医院。头部受伤和内出血会在数小时后才显现，而且这里的炎热天气会让路面擦伤很快感染。',
  'Get a police report. Without one, most travel insurance and every vehicle claim is disputed. Ask for the report number before you leave.': '取得警方报告。没有报告，大多数旅行保险和所有车辆索赔都会被拒绝。离开前请索取报告编号。',
  'Photograph everything at the scene: both vehicles, the road, the position, any licence and registration, and the other rider. Photographs settle later arguments that memory cannot.': '拍下现场的一切：两辆车、道路、车辆位置、任何驾照和行驶证，以及另一位骑手。照片能解决记忆无法解决的日后争执。',
  'Tell your insurer the same day. Many policies exclude motorcycle injury unless you hold a licence valid for that engine size and were wearing a helmet — know which before you rent, not after you crash.': '当天就告知您的保险公司。许多保单会免责摩托车受伤，除非您持有适用于该排量的有效驾照并戴了头盔，请在租车前而不是出事后弄清楚。',
  'Do not hand over your passport as security to a rental shop, a hospital or anyone at the scene. Offer a photocopy or a deposit instead — a withheld passport is the standard lever in a rental dispute.': '不要把护照交给租车店、医院或现场任何人作抵押。请改为提供复印件或押金，扣留护照是租车纠纷中常见的手段。',
  'Do not agree a cash settlement at the roadside before you know the extent of your own injuries.': '在弄清自己的伤情之前，不要在路边同意现金和解。',
  'Drink spiking & methanol poisoning': '被下药与甲醇中毒',
  'Rare but not hypothetical — and methanol poisoning is survivable only if it is recognised early.': '罕见但并非不可能，甲醇中毒只有及早识别才能存活。',
  'Treat sudden severe drunkenness that does not match how much was drunk as an emergency, especially after free shots, mixed spirits or home-made liquor.': '如果突然出现严重醉酒，与饮酒量不相符，请视为紧急情况，尤其是在喝了免费烈酒、混合烈酒或自酿酒之后。',
  'Methanol poisoning classically appears 6–30 hours after drinking, not immediately: blurred or snowy vision, severe stomach pain, breathlessness, confusion. Any vision change after drinking spirits is a hospital emergency that night, not in the morning.': '甲醇中毒通常在饮酒后 6 至 30 小时出现，而不是立刻出现：视物模糊或像下雪、严重胃痛、呼吸困难、意识混乱。饮用烈酒后出现任何视力变化，都应当晚就去医院，而不是等到早上。',
  'Get the person to the largest hospital you can reach and say the words "possible methanol poisoning". Treatment exists and works; delay is what kills.': '把此人送往您能到达的最大的医院，并说出“可能是甲醇中毒”。治疗是存在且有效的，致命的是延误。',
  'If someone is unconscious but breathing, put them on their side so they cannot choke, and stay with them.': '如果有人昏迷但仍有呼吸，请让其侧卧以免窒息，并留在其身边。',
  'Keep the bottle, the glass or the receipt if you safely can — it helps the hospital and any investigation.': '如果能安全地做到，请保留酒瓶、杯子或收据，这对医院和任何调查都有帮助。',
  'Report it to the tourist police and to your embassy. Clusters are how these venues get shut.': '请向旅游警察和您的使馆报告。正是因为有这类聚集案例，这些场所才会被关停。',
  'Do not let anyone "sleep it off" alone in a room. Almost every death in a spiking or methanol cluster involves someone left to sleep.': '不要让任何人独自在房间里“睡一觉就好”。几乎每一起下药或甲醇事件中的死亡，都涉及被留下独自睡觉的人。',
  'Do not accept drinks from a shared jug or a bucket you did not watch being poured, and do not leave a drink unattended.': '不要接受来自共用酒壶或您没有亲眼看着倒的酒桶的饮品，也不要让饮品无人看管。',
  'Lost or stolen passport': '护照遗失或被盗',
  'Recoverable, but the order of the steps decides whether it takes two days or two weeks.': '可以补办，但步骤的顺序决定了需要两天还是两周。',
  'Report it to the local police and get a written report with a reference number. Every embassy asks for it, and so does your insurer.': '向当地警方报案，并取得带编号的书面报告。每个使馆都会要求提供，您的保险公司也是如此。',
  'Contact your embassy or consulate — the nearest one is usually in Bangkok, Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City or Phnom Penh, and many countries have none at all in Laos.': '联系您的使馆或领事馆，最近的通常在曼谷、河内、胡志明市或金边，而在老挝，许多国家根本没有。',
  'If your visa or entry stamp was in it, immigration will need to reissue the record before you can leave the country. Start that on the same day.': '如果您的签证或入境章在护照里，移民部门需要先重新签发该记录，您才能离开该国。请当天就着手办理。',
  'Ask for an emergency travel document if you have a flight soon; a full replacement passport takes longer and may have to be issued from a regional hub.': '如果您很快有航班，请申请紧急旅行证件；完整补办护照需要更长时间，还可能需要由区域中心签发。',
  'Cancel and replace any cards that went with it, and change the passwords for anything that was unlocked on a stolen phone.': '注销并补办与护照一起丢失的任何银行卡，并更改在被盗手机上处于解锁状态的所有账户的密码。',
  'Do not leave the country by land while the entry record is unresolved — an unmatched entry stamp turns a lost passport into an immigration problem.': '入境记录尚未解决时，不要从陆路出境，对不上的入境章会把护照遗失变成移民问题。',
  'Do not rely on the photocopy alone. Keep a photograph of the data page and the entry stamp somewhere you can reach without your phone.': '不要只依赖复印件。请把资料页和入境章的照片保存在无需手机就能取到的地方。',
  'Robbery, theft or assault': '抢劫、盗窃或袭击',
  'Snatch theft from a moving motorbike is the common version, and it injures people because they hold on.': '最常见的是在行驶的摩托车上抢夺，而且因为受害者紧抓不放而导致受伤。',
  'Let it go. A bag is replaceable; being dragged along a road is how snatch theft causes serious injury and death.': '放手吧。包可以再买，被拖在路上则是抢夺造成重伤和死亡的原因。',
  'If you are hurt, treat that first and go to hospital — the report can be made afterwards.': '如果您受伤了，请先处理伤势并去医院，报案可以之后再做。',
  'Report it to the tourist police where there is a tourist police unit; they usually have English speakers and handle traveller cases directly.': '在设有旅游警察的地方，请向旅游警察报案；他们通常有会说英语的人员，并直接处理旅行者案件。',
  'Freeze cards immediately and check for transactions — card cloning at ATMs is common in this region.': '立即冻结银行卡并检查交易，在这一地区，ATM 上的盗刷克隆很常见。',
  'Get the written police report for your insurer; a verbal report is not enough for a claim.': '为保险公司取得书面警方报告；口头报案不足以索赔。',
  'Tell your embassy if a passport, a visa or your safety is involved.': '如果涉及护照、签证或您的人身安全，请告知您的使馆。',
  'Do not chase anyone, and do not confront a group.': '不要追赶任何人，也不要与一群人对峙。',
  'Do not carry your only card, your only phone and your passport in the same bag.': '不要把唯一的银行卡、唯一的手机和护照放在同一个包里。',
  'Arrested or detained': '被逮捕或拘留',
  'Drug offences carry severe penalties across all four countries, including sentences travellers do not expect.': '毒品犯罪在四个国家都会面临严厉处罚，包括旅行者意想不到的刑期。',
  'Ask immediately, clearly and repeatedly to contact your embassy. You are entitled to consular access; the request is what triggers it.': '请立即、清楚且反复要求联系您的使馆。您有权获得领事探视，提出要求才会触发这一程序。',
  'Do not sign anything you cannot read, and say so plainly. Ask for a translated copy and for a lawyer.': '不要签署您看不懂的任何文件，并明确说明这一点。请要求提供翻译件并要求律师。',
  'Stay calm and polite. Argument and raised voices make everything that follows harder.': '保持冷静和礼貌。争吵和提高嗓门会让之后的一切更加困难。',
  'The embassy can supply a list of local lawyers, contact your family and monitor your treatment.': '使馆可以提供当地律师名单，联系您的家人，并关注您受到的对待。',
  'Arrange money through family or your insurer rather than through anyone who approaches you at the station.': '请通过家人或保险公司安排资金，而不要通过在警察局里主动接近您的任何人。',
  'Do not offer money to a police officer. In a genuine arrest it converts a bad situation into a far worse one.': '不要向警察提供金钱。在真正的逮捕中，这会把糟糕的情况变得更糟。',
  'Do not assume a substance is legal because it is sold openly to tourists — cannabis law in Thailand has changed more than once and differs completely in the other three countries.': '不要因为某种物质向游客公开出售，就认为它是合法的：泰国的大麻法律已多次变动，而其他三个国家则完全不同。',
  'In trouble in the water': '在水中遇险',
  'Drowning is the second leading cause of traveller death here, and rip currents cause most of it.': '溺水是这里旅行者死亡的第二大原因，其中大部分由离岸流造成。',
  'Caught in a rip: do not swim against it. Float, signal, and swim parallel to the beach until the pull stops, then come in at an angle.': '被卷入离岸流：不要逆流游。保持漂浮、发出信号，并平行于海滩游动，直到拉力消失，然后斜向游回岸边。',
  'Helping someone else: throw them something that floats and call for help. Swimming out to a panicking person is how one drowning becomes two.': '帮助他人：扔给对方可漂浮的东西并呼救。游向惊慌的人，会使一人溺水变成两人溺水。',
  'Out of the water and not breathing: start chest compressions immediately — hard and fast in the centre of the chest, about twice a second — and send someone for an ambulance.': '已上岸但没有呼吸：立即开始胸外按压，在胸部中央用力快速按压，每秒约两次，并派人去叫救护车。',
  'Anyone who has been under the water needs hospital assessment even if they seem fine afterwards.': '任何曾沉入水下的人，即使事后看起来没事，也需要到医院评估。',
  'For a jellyfish sting, flood the area with vinegar for at least thirty seconds and treat any breathing difficulty as an emergency. Box jellyfish are present in the Gulf of Thailand and around the Cambodian coast.': '被水母蜇伤时，用醋冲洗该区域至少三十秒，并把任何呼吸困难视为紧急情况。泰国湾和柬埔寨海岸一带有箱形水母。',
  'Do not swim where a red flag is flying, and do not judge a beach by how calm it looks — rips are strongest where the water appears flattest.': '不要在飘着红旗的地方游泳，也不要凭海滩看起来平静来判断，水面看似最平的地方离岸流最强。',
  'Do not drink and swim, and do not swim alone at night.': '不要饮酒后游泳，也不要夜间独自游泳。',
  'High fever': '高烧',
  'Dengue is the biggest infectious risk to travellers in this region, and it is seasonal rather than rare.': '登革热是这一地区旅行者面临的最大传染病风险，它具有季节性，并不罕见。',
  'Any fever above 38 °C that lasts more than 24 hours needs a doctor and a blood test. Dengue, malaria and typhoid all start looking like flu.': '任何超过 38 °C 并持续超过 24 小时的发烧，都需要看医生并验血。登革热、疟疾和伤寒起初都像流感。',
  'Take paracetamol for fever and pain — nothing else.': '发烧和疼痛请服用对乙酰氨基酚，不要服用其他药物。',
  'Drink steadily. Dehydration is what turns a manageable dengue into an admission.': '要持续补水。脱水会让可控的登革热变成需要住院。',
  'Warning signs that mean hospital now, not tomorrow: severe stomach pain, repeated vomiting, bleeding gums or nose, black stools, breathlessness, or a sudden drop in temperature with cold clammy skin.': '意味着应立即而不是明天去医院的警示症状：剧烈胃痛、反复呕吐、牙龈或鼻出血、黑便、呼吸困难，或体温骤降并伴有皮肤冰冷湿黏。',
  'Malaria is a risk in forested border areas rather than the cities. Tell the doctor exactly where you have been in the last month.': '疟疾的风险在森林边境地区，而不是城市。请准确告诉医生您过去一个月去过哪里。',
  'Do not take ibuprofen, aspirin or any other anti-inflammatory until dengue has been ruled out — they increase bleeding risk.': '在排除登革热之前，不要服用布洛芬、阿司匹林或任何其他消炎药，它们会增加出血风险。',
  'Do not buy antimalarials or antibiotics from a small shop; counterfeit medicine is a genuine problem outside established pharmacies.': '不要从小店购买抗疟药或抗生素；在正规药房以外，假药确实是个问题。',
  'Severe stomach illness': '严重的胃肠疾病',
  'Common, usually self-limiting, and occasionally the thing that puts a traveller on a drip.': '常见，通常可自行缓解，偶尔会让旅行者需要输液。',
  'Rehydrate with oral rehydration salts, sold in every pharmacy in the region. Water alone does not replace what is being lost.': '用口服补液盐补水，本地区所有药店都有售。仅喝水无法补充流失的成分。',
  'Small sips, often, are better tolerated than a glass at a time.': '少量多次饮用，比一次喝一杯更容易耐受。',
  'See a doctor if there is blood in the stool, a fever above 38.5 °C, vomiting that stops you keeping fluids down, or symptoms lasting more than three days.': '如果大便带血、发烧超过 38.5 °C、呕吐导致无法保持摄入液体，或症状持续超过三天，请就医。',
  'A young child, an older traveller or anyone pregnant should be seen much sooner than that.': '幼儿、年长的旅行者或孕妇应更早就医。',
  'Do not take a stop-the-symptoms antidiarrhoeal if there is blood or a high fever — it can make the underlying infection worse.': '如果有血便或高烧，不要服用止泻药，它可能使潜在的感染恶化。',
  'Flood, storm, earthquake or tsunami': '洪水、风暴、地震或海啸',
  'The regional hazards are seasonal flooding, tropical storms, and — on the Andaman coast — tsunami.': '本地区的灾害有季节性洪水、热带风暴，以及在安达曼海岸的海啸。',
  'Feel a strong earthquake on the coast, or see the sea suddenly draw back? Move inland and uphill immediately and do not wait for an official warning. On the Andaman coast, follow the blue tsunami evacuation signs.': '在海岸感到强烈地震，或看到海水突然退去？请立即向内陆和高处转移，不要等待官方警报。在安达曼海岸，请跟随蓝色的海啸疏散标志。',
  'Flooding: never walk or drive through moving water. Thirty centimetres will float a car and knee-deep flow will take an adult off their feet. Flash floods in the northern gorges rise in minutes.': '洪水：切勿徒步或驾车穿过流动的水。三十厘米的水就能让汽车浮起，齐膝深的水流就能把成年人冲倒。北部峡谷的山洪几分钟内就会上涨。',
  'Storm: get indoors and away from windows, trees and hoardings. Boat services stop for a reason — do not press a captain to sail.': '风暴：请进入室内，远离窗户、树木和广告牌。船班停运自有原因，不要催促船长开船。',
  'Assume the water is contaminated after any flood, and treat every cut and graze that touched it.': '任何洪水过后，都应假定水已受到污染，并处理每一处接触过水的割伤和擦伤。',
  'Register with your embassy’s travel service if one is available, so you can be contacted during a large event.': '如有可能，请在您使馆的旅行服务中登记，以便在大型事件中能联系到您。',
  'Do not rely on mobile coverage during a major event; agree a meeting point with anyone you are travelling with in advance.': '大型事件期间不要依赖手机信号；请提前与同行的人约定集合地点。',
  'Fire in a hotel or hostel': '酒店或青年旅舍起火',
  'Older guesthouses across the region often have one staircase, barred windows and no working alarm.': '本地区较老的旅馆往往只有一条楼梯、有栏杆的窗户，并且没有可用的警报器。',
  'Get out and stay out. Do not stop for luggage.': '出去，并且不要再回去。不要停下来拿行李。',
  'Stay low under smoke, and feel a door with the back of your hand before opening it.': '在烟雾中保持低姿，开门前先用手背试一试门的温度。',
  'If you cannot get out, close the door, block the gap with wet cloth, get to a window and make yourself visible.': '如果出不去，请关上门，用湿布堵住缝隙，走到窗边并让人看到您。',
  'Account for everyone you are travelling with at a point away from the building.': '在远离建筑的地方清点所有同行的人。',
  'Do not use a lift. Check where the stairs are on the night you arrive — it takes ten seconds and it is the whole of fire safety in a strange building.': '不要使用电梯。到达的当晚就看一下楼梯在哪里，这只需十秒钟，却是陌生建筑里消防安全的全部。',
  'Someone you are travelling with is missing': '与您同行的人失踪了',
  'Report it to the police immediately. There is no waiting period, and the first hours matter most.': '请立即向警方报案。没有等待期，最初的几个小时最关键。',
  'Contact your embassy at the same time — they can press a case that a local station may otherwise treat as routine.': '同时联系您的使馆，他们可以推动一桩当地警局可能当作例行公事处理的案件。',
  'Check the hospitals in the area as well as the police; someone brought in unconscious and without documents may not be identified for a while.': '除了警方之外，还要查看该地区的医院；被送来时昏迷且没有证件的人，可能很久都无法确认身份。',
  'Gather a recent photograph, what they were wearing, their phone number and any location-sharing they had switched on.': '收集一张近照、其穿着、其电话号码，以及其开启的任何位置共享信息。',
  'Ask their accommodation, their last known driver or boat operator, and the last place they were seen. Local businesses often know more than a station does.': '询问其住宿处、最后已知的司机或船夫，以及最后一次被看到的地点。当地商家往往比警局知道得更多。',
  'Do not delay to "give it another day". The advice from every consular service is to report early and stand it down later if it was nothing.': '不要拖延“再等一天”。每个领事部门的建议都是尽早报案，如果没事再撤销。',
  'A mental health crisis': '心理健康危机',
  'Long trips, isolation, heat, drink and sleeplessness make this more common on the road than at home.': '长途旅行、孤立、炎热、饮酒和失眠，使这种情况在旅途中比在家里更常见。',
  'If someone is at immediate risk of harming themselves, do not leave them alone, and call the national emergency number.': '如果有人面临立即伤害自己的风险，请不要让其独处，并拨打全国紧急电话。',
  'Get to a hospital emergency department; the larger private hospitals in Bangkok, Ho Chi Minh City, Hanoi and Phnom Penh have psychiatric services, most public provincial hospitals do not.': '前往医院急诊科；曼谷、胡志明市、河内和金边较大的私立医院设有精神科服务，大多数省级公立医院没有。',
  'Remove the immediate means of harm if you can do so safely.': '如果能安全地做到，请移除可能立即造成伤害的物品。',
  'Your travel insurer’s assistance line can arrange a psychiatric referral and, where needed, a medically escorted flight home.': '您的旅行保险公司的援助热线可以安排精神科转诊，必要时安排有医护陪同的回国航班。',
  'Your embassy can contact family and help with practical arrangements.': '您的使馆可以联系家人，并协助处理实际安排。',
  'Local mental health services are limited in Cambodia and Laos in particular; getting to a major city, or home, is often the realistic plan.': '尤其是在柬埔寨和老挝，当地心理健康服务有限；前往大城市或回国往往是现实的方案。',
  'Do not treat "they have been drinking" as an explanation that makes it less urgent.': '不要把“他们喝了酒”当作让事情不那么紧急的解释。',
  'If a traveller dies': '如果有旅行者去世',
  'The hardest page here, written down so nobody has to work it out while grieving.': '这里最沉重的一页，写下来是为了让没有人需要在悲痛中自己摸索该怎么办。',
  'Contact your embassy or consulate first. Repatriation, local registration of the death and the paperwork all run through them, and they will explain the order of it.': '首先联系您的使馆或领事馆。遗体送返、当地死亡登记和各项文件都通过他们办理，他们会解释先后顺序。',
  'Contact the travel insurer. Repatriation of remains is expensive and is the single most valuable thing a policy covers.': '联系旅行保险公司。遗体送返费用昂贵，是保单承保的最有价值的一项。',
  'A local death certificate is issued by the authorities where the death occurred; the embassy can advise on getting it recognised at home.': '当地死亡证明由死亡发生地的当局签发；使馆可就如何在国内获得承认提供建议。',
  'Do not agree to a cremation or a burial before speaking to the embassy and the family — in some countries it cannot be undone or reversed.': '在与使馆和家人商量之前，不要同意火化或土葬，在某些国家，这是无法撤销或逆转的。',
  'Issue an emergency travel document or a replacement passport.': '签发紧急旅行证件或补发护照。',
  'Contact your family and help you get money sent to you.': '联系您的家人，并帮助您接收汇款。',
  'Visit you and monitor your treatment if you are arrested or detained.': '如果您被逮捕或拘留，探视您并关注您受到的对待。',
  'Give you a list of local lawyers, translators and doctors.': '给您提供当地律师、翻译和医生的名单。',
  'Help in a death, a serious accident, or a large-scale emergency.': '协助处理死亡、严重事故或大规模紧急事件。',
  'Give you the current official travel and health advice for where you are.': '提供您所在地当前的官方旅行和健康建议。',
  'Get you out of prison, or interfere in a local investigation or court case.': '把您从监狱中救出，或干预当地的调查或法庭案件。',
  'Pay your medical bills, your legal costs or your fare home.': '支付您的医疗费、法律费用或回程机票。',
  'Investigate a crime, or make the police act faster than local law allows.': '调查犯罪，或让警方比当地法律允许的更快采取行动。',
  'Give you legal or medical advice of its own.': '自行为您提供法律或医疗建议。',
  'Many countries have an embassy in Bangkok, Hanoi and Phnom Penh but none at all in Vientiane — in Laos your nearest consular help is often in Bangkok. Find yours, and save the address and the emergency line, before you need it.': '许多国家在曼谷、河内和金边设有使馆，但在万象完全没有，在老挝，您最近的领事协助通常在曼谷。请在需要之前，找到您的使馆，并保存其地址和紧急热线。',
  '24h emergency': '24 小时急诊',
  'Children': '儿童',
  'Maternity': '产科',
  'English / international': '英语 / 国际服务',
  'Major trauma & surgery': '重大创伤与外科',
  'Hyperbaric (dive) chamber': '高压氧舱（潜水）',
  'Arranges medical evacuation': '安排医疗后送',
  'Not responding, or not breathing normally': '无反应，或呼吸不正常',
  'Allergic reaction & breathing emergencies': '过敏反应与呼吸急症',
  'Bleeding, shock, burns & collapse': '出血、休克、烧伤与昏倒',
  'Heart, stroke & blood sugar': '心脏、中风与血糖',
  'Babies & children — everyday emergencies': '婴幼儿：常见急症',
  'Snakes, marine life & animal bites': '蛇、海洋生物与动物咬伤',
  'Water, weather & getting help': '水、天气与获取帮助',
  'Someone collapses, or will not wake up': '有人昏倒，或叫不醒',
  'Check for a response — speak loudly and gently shake their shoulders (a baby: tap the foot, do not shake).': '检查有无反应：大声说话并轻拍其肩膀（婴儿：拍打脚底，不要摇晃）。',
  'If they respond and are breathing normally: do not move them if you suspect a neck or back injury; otherwise put them in the recovery position (below) and keep checking their breathing.': '如果对方有反应且呼吸正常：若怀疑颈部或背部受伤，请不要移动；否则让其采取复原卧位（见下文），并持续观察呼吸。',
  'If they do NOT respond: shout for help, and check breathing for up to 10 seconds — look, listen, feel. Noisy, gasping or irregular breathing counts as "not breathing normally".': '如果对方没有反应：大声呼救，并检查呼吸最多 10 秒：看、听、感觉。有杂音、喘息或不规则的呼吸都算作“呼吸不正常”。',
  'Not breathing, or not breathing normally: call the emergency number on speakerphone (or send someone to) and start CPR immediately — see the adult/child or baby steps below. Do not wait to find a pulse; lay rescuers are not asked to check for one.': '没有呼吸或呼吸不正常：用免提拨打紧急电话（或让人去打），并立即开始心肺复苏，参见下方成人 / 儿童或婴儿的步骤。不要等着去摸脉搏，非专业施救者不需要检查脉搏。',
  'Send someone to find an AED (defibrillator) if one might be nearby — large hotels, malls and airports sometimes have one.': '如果附近可能有 AED（除颤器），请让人去找，大型酒店、商场和机场有时设有。',
  'CPR — adult and child over about 1 year': '心肺复苏：成人和约 1 岁以上儿童',
  'Lay them on their back on a firm, flat surface.': '让其仰卧在坚硬平整的表面上。',
  'Heel of one hand on the centre of the chest (lower half of the breastbone); for a child, one or two hands depending on their size.': '一只手的掌根放在胸部中央（胸骨下半部）；儿童视体型使用一只或两只手。',
  'Push hard and fast: adult depth 5–6 cm, child about one-third of the chest’s depth (roughly 5 cm) — both at 100–120 pushes per minute, letting the chest fully rise between pushes.': '用力快速按压：成人按压深度 5–6 厘米，儿童约为胸廓深度的三分之一（约 5 厘米），频率均为每分钟 100–120 次，每次按压之间让胸廓完全回弹。',
  'If trained and willing: 30 pushes, then 2 rescue breaths, repeating (children may be given 15:2 if there are two trained rescuers). If untrained, unwilling, or unable to give breaths: continuous push-only CPR is still far better than nothing.': '如果受过训练且愿意：按压 30 次，然后人工呼吸 2 次，循环进行（如有两位受过训练的施救者，儿童可用 15:2）。如果未受训练、不愿意或无法做人工呼吸：持续只做按压的心肺复苏仍远好于什么都不做。',
  'Use an AED the moment one arrives and follow its voice prompts — it will not shock unless a shock is needed.': 'AED 一到就立即使用，并遵循其语音提示，只有在需要电击时它才会电击。',
  'Keep going until the person starts breathing normally, professional help takes over, or you are physically unable to continue.': '持续进行，直到对方恢复正常呼吸、专业人员接手，或您体力不支无法继续。',
  'Alone with no phone: with an adult, call first, then start CPR. With a child, current guidance is to give CPR for about one to two minutes first if you truly cannot call and compress at the same time (put the phone on speaker and start compressions the moment you have dialled, if that is possible instead).': '独自一人且没有手机：对成人，先打电话，再开始心肺复苏。对儿童，现行指南是如果确实无法同时打电话和按压，先做约一到两分钟的心肺复苏（如果可能，改为把手机开免提，拨通后立刻开始按压）。',
  'A rescuer taught with breaths first (5 initial breaths before compressions, still taught in the UK/Europe for children) and one taught compressions-first (the US/AHA approach) are both following a currently-endorsed method — do not hesitate over which to use.': '先做人工呼吸的施救者（按压前先做 5 次初始呼吸，英国 / 欧洲对儿童仍这样教）和先按压的施救者（美国 / AHA 方法）都遵循目前认可的方法，不要在用哪种上犹豫。',
  'CPR — baby under 1 year': '心肺复苏：1 岁以下婴儿',
  'Lay the baby on their back on a firm surface, head in a neutral position (not tilted back).': '让婴儿仰卧在坚硬表面上，头部保持中立位置（不要后仰）。',
  'For rescue breaths, your mouth covers the baby’s mouth AND nose.': '做人工呼吸时，您的嘴要同时盖住婴儿的口和鼻。',
  'Compress the lower half of the breastbone, just below the nipple line, using two thumbs wrapped around the chest (preferred where you can manage it) or the heel of one hand if you cannot encircle the chest — two fingers is also still taught in some countries and is not wrong if that is what you learned.': '按压胸骨下半部，位于乳头连线正下方，用两个拇指环绕胸部按压（如能做到则为首选），如果无法环抱胸部，则用一只手的掌根，有些国家仍教用两根手指，如果您学的是这种方法，也没有错。',
  'Push at least one-third of the chest’s depth (about 4 cm), 100–120 per minute.': '按压深度至少为胸廓深度的三分之一（约 4 厘米），每分钟 100–120 次。',
  '30 compressions to 2 breaths for a single rescuer; 15:2 if there are two trained rescuers.': '单人施救按压 30 次、人工呼吸 2 次；如有两位受过训练的施救者则为 15:2。',
  'Keep going until the baby responds, help takes over, or you cannot continue.': '持续进行，直到婴儿有反应、专业人员接手，或您无法继续。',
  'Which hand technique is "correct" is genuinely still shifting between countries as of 2026 — two-thumb encircling is now preferred almost everywhere, but two-finger and heel-of-one-hand are still taught and are not mistakes.': '到 2026 年，哪种手法才是“正确的”在各国之间仍在变化：目前几乎各地都首选双拇指环抱法，但双指法和单手掌根法仍有教授，也不算错误。',
  'Choking — adult and child over about 1 year': '噎食：成人和约 1 岁以上儿童',
  'If they can cough, speak or breathe: encourage coughing and do nothing else yet.': '如果对方能咳嗽、说话或呼吸：鼓励其咳嗽，暂时不要做其他事。',
  'If they cannot cough, speak or breathe: give up to 5 firm blows between the shoulder blades with the heel of your hand.': '如果对方无法咳嗽、说话或呼吸：用手掌根在两肩胛骨之间用力拍击最多 5 次。',
  'Not cleared: give up to 5 abdominal thrusts — stand behind them, fist just above the navel, pull sharply inward and upward. (Some countries — Australia and New Zealand — teach chest thrusts instead of abdominal thrusts; both are recognised as effective.)': '未排出：做最多 5 次腹部冲击，站在其身后，拳头放在肚脐上方，向内向上猛力拉。（有些国家，如澳大利亚和新西兰，教的是胸部冲击而不是腹部冲击，两者都被认为有效。）',
  'Keep alternating 5 back blows with 5 thrusts until the object clears or the person becomes unresponsive.': '继续交替进行 5 次背部拍击和 5 次冲击，直到异物排出或对方失去反应。',
  'If they become unresponsive: lower them to the ground and start CPR (above) — look in the mouth each time you open the airway and only remove an object you can actually see.': '如果对方失去反应：让其平躺到地上并开始心肺复苏（见上文），每次打开气道时都查看口腔，只取出您确实能看到的异物。',
  'Anyone who was given abdominal thrusts should see a doctor afterwards, even once the object is out — they can cause internal injury.': '接受过腹部冲击的人事后应就医，即使异物已经排出，因为腹部冲击可能造成内伤。',
  'Never do a blind finger sweep of the mouth.': '切勿盲目用手指在口中探挖。',
  'Choking — baby under 1 year': '噎食：1 岁以下婴儿',
  'Lay the baby face down along your forearm or thigh, head lower than their chest, supporting the head and jaw.': '让婴儿脸朝下趴在您的前臂或大腿上，头低于胸部，并托住头部和下颌。',
  'Give up to 5 firm back blows between the shoulder blades with the heel of your hand, checking between each.': '用手掌根在两肩胛骨之间用力拍击最多 5 次，每次之后都检查。',
  'Not cleared: turn the baby face up (still head-down along your arm/thigh) and give up to 5 chest thrusts on the lower half of the breastbone, just below the nipple line — two fingers, two thumbs, or the heel of one hand are all currently taught; use whichever you know.': '未排出：把婴儿翻成脸朝上（仍然头低位，趴在您的手臂 / 大腿上），在胸骨下半部、乳头连线正下方做最多 5 次胸部冲击，两根手指、两个拇指或单手掌根目前都有教授，用您熟悉的即可。',
  'Keep alternating 5 back blows with 5 chest thrusts.': '继续交替进行 5 次背部拍击和 5 次胸部冲击。',
  'If the baby becomes unresponsive: start baby CPR (above) and get emergency help.': '如果婴儿失去反应：开始婴儿心肺复苏（见上文）并获取紧急救援。',
  'Never give abdominal thrusts to a baby — real risk of internal injury.': '切勿对婴儿做腹部冲击，有造成内伤的实际风险。',
  'Never do a blind finger sweep; only remove an object you can actually see.': '切勿盲目用手指探挖，只取出您确实能看到的异物。',
  'Recovery position': '复原卧位',
  'For someone unresponsive but breathing normally, with no reason to suspect CPR or serious bleeding is needed: roll them onto their side and tilt the head back slightly, so the airway stays open and fluid can drain out. Do not put them on their back.': '对于无反应但呼吸正常、且没有理由怀疑需要心肺复苏或严重出血的人：让其侧卧并稍微后仰头部，使气道保持通畅，液体可以流出。不要让其仰卧。',
  'A baby: do not put them on the floor — hold them face down along your forearm, head supported and tilted a little lower than the body.': '婴儿：不要放在地板上，让其脸朝下趴在您的前臂上，托住头部，并让头比身体稍低。',
  'Keep watching their breathing until help arrives. Noisy, irregular or gasping breathing is a sign to treat them as not breathing and start CPR instead.': '在救援到达前持续观察其呼吸。有杂音、不规则或喘息式呼吸，说明应当视为没有呼吸并改做心肺复苏。',
  'A pregnant woman should go on her LEFT side.': '孕妇应取左侧卧位。',
  'Drowning': '溺水',
  'Do not swim out to them unless you are trained for water rescue — reach with a pole, branch or rope, or throw something that floats, instead.': '除非受过水上救援训练，否则不要游向对方，请改用杆子、树枝或绳子够到对方，或扔给对方可漂浮的东西。',
  'Once they are out of the water and not breathing normally: open the airway and give a few rescue breaths (guidance ranges from 2 to 5; 5 is now the most common number taught), then continue CPR at the normal ratio (30 compressions to 2 breaths).': '对方出水后如果呼吸不正常：打开气道并做几次人工呼吸（指南从 2 次到 5 次不等，5 次是目前最常教的数字），然后按正常比例（按压 30 次、人工呼吸 2 次）继续心肺复苏。',
  'Untrained, unwilling or unable to give breaths: compression-only CPR is still far better than nothing, but breaths genuinely improve survival after drowning specifically, more than in an ordinary adult cardiac arrest — give them if you can.': '未受训练、不愿意或无法做人工呼吸：只做按压的心肺复苏仍远好于什么都不做，但人工呼吸确实能提高溺水后的存活率，尤其是比普通成人心脏骤停更明显，请尽量做。',
  'Vomiting is common during resuscitation — be ready to roll the person onto their side and clear the mouth, then continue.': '复苏期间常会呕吐，请做好准备，把对方翻成侧卧并清理口腔，然后继续。',
  'Everyone who was pulled from the water unresponsive, needed rescue breaths or CPR, or has any cough, breathlessness, confusion or drowsiness afterwards must be seen at a hospital, even if they seem to recover — a delayed reaction (secondary drowning) is real.': '所有被从水中救起时无反应、需要人工呼吸或心肺复苏，或事后出现任何咳嗽、呼吸急促、意识混乱或嗜睡的人，即使看似恢复也必须到医院检查，延迟反应（继发性溺水）是真实存在的。',
  'Recognise anaphylaxis (severe allergic reaction)': '识别过敏性休克（严重过敏反应）',
  'Sudden breathing or circulation trouble after a food, sting or medicine: swelling of the tongue or throat, noisy or difficult breathing, a wheeze or persistent cough, a hoarse voice, difficulty swallowing, dizziness or collapse.': '在食用食物、被蜇或服药后突然出现呼吸或循环问题：舌头或喉咙肿胀、呼吸有杂音或困难、喘鸣或持续咳嗽、声音嘶哑、吞咽困难、头晕或昏倒。',
  'Often — but not always — with hives or skin swelling. A reaction can be severe with no skin signs at all.': '常伴有荨麻疹或皮肤肿胀，但并非总是如此。反应可能很严重，却没有任何皮肤表现。',
  'In babies and young children specifically: sudden pale, floppy or limp, not responding normally.': '尤其是婴幼儿：突然脸色苍白、软绵绵或瘫软、反应不正常。',
  'Anaphylaxis — what to do': '过敏性休克：该怎么做',
  'If an adrenaline (epinephrine) auto-injector is available, use it AT ONCE into the outer mid-thigh — through clothing is fine.': '如有肾上腺素自动注射器，请立即注射在大腿外侧中部，隔着衣服也可以。',
  'Call the emergency number straight away.': '立即拨打紧急电话。',
  'Lie the person flat and raise their legs; if breathing is very hard, let them sit up instead. Someone pregnant should lie on her left side.': '让对方平躺并抬高双腿；如果呼吸非常困难，则让其坐起。孕妇应左侧卧。',
  'Do not let them stand or walk, even once they feel better — a sudden drop in blood pressure while upright can be fatal.': '不要让其站立或走动，即使感觉好转，直立时血压骤降可能致命。',
  'No improvement after about 5 minutes and a second auto-injector is available: give the second dose.': '约 5 分钟后仍无改善且有第二支自动注射器：注射第二剂。',
  'Go to hospital every time, even after a full recovery — symptoms can return hours later (a biphasic reaction).': '每次都要去医院，即使完全恢复，症状也可能在数小时后复发（双相反应）。',
  'If in genuine doubt whether it is anaphylaxis, every source agrees: give the adrenaline. The risk of a dose given when it was not strictly needed is far smaller than the risk of withholding it when it was.': '如果真的拿不准是否为过敏性休克，所有来源都一致认为：注射肾上腺素。在并非严格需要时注射一剂的风险，远小于在需要时不注射的风险。',
  'Anaphylaxis in babies and children': '婴幼儿过敏性休克',
  'Lay a baby or toddler flat — never hold them upright.': '让婴儿或幼儿平躺，切勿竖抱。',
  'Use their own prescribed auto-injector at its prescribed dose the moment anaphylaxis is suspected.': '一旦怀疑过敏性休克，立即按处方剂量使用其本人的处方自动注射器。',
  'Auto-injector doses run roughly: 0.1 mg for about 7.5–15 kg (where that device exists), 0.15 mg from about 7.5–20 kg up to 30 kg depending on country and device, 0.3 mg above about 20–30 kg.': '自动注射器的剂量大致为：约 7.5–15 公斤用 0.1 毫克（该型号存在的情况下），约 7.5–20 公斤至 30 公斤用 0.15 毫克（因国家和器械而异），约 20–30 公斤以上用 0.3 毫克。',
  'Under about 7.5 kg, or any child with no prescribed device: call the emergency number immediately and let paramedics or a doctor decide the dose — do not improvise with a mismatched adult device.': '体重约 7.5 公斤以下，或没有处方器械的任何儿童：请立即拨打紧急电话，由急救人员或医生决定剂量，不要随意使用不匹配的成人器械。',
  'Dosing bands genuinely differ between countries and auto-injector brands — this is not a single fixed number worldwide. Always follow the child’s own prescribed device and plan where one exists.': '各国和各品牌自动注射器的剂量区间确实有差异，全球并没有统一的固定数值。如有该儿童自己的处方器械和方案，请始终遵循。',
  'Asthma attack': '哮喘发作',
  'Help them sit upright — never lie them down. Stay calm; anxiety worsens breathing.': '帮助其坐直，切勿让其躺下。保持冷静，焦虑会加重呼吸困难。',
  'Use the blue/grey reliever inhaler at once, with a spacer if one is available.': '立即使用蓝色 / 灰色的缓解型吸入器，如有储雾罐请配合使用。',
  'They have their own written asthma action plan: follow its dosing exactly.': '如果对方有自己的书面哮喘行动计划：请严格按其剂量执行。',
  'No plan: either recognised approach is safe — 1 puff every 30–60 seconds up to 10 puffs (UK-style), or 4 puffs (one at a time via a spacer, 4 breaths each), wait 4 minutes, then repeat (Australia-style).': '没有计划：两种公认的方法都是安全的：每 30–60 秒吸 1 次，最多 10 次（英国方式），或吸 4 次（通过储雾罐每次一喷，各呼吸 4 次），等待 4 分钟后重复（澳大利亚方式）。',
  'Call the emergency number if: there is no inhaler, the inhaler is not helping, lips or fingers turn blue, the person is exhausted or confused, breathing becomes quiet or slow, or symptoms have not resolved after the full first round.': '出现以下情况请拨打紧急电话：没有吸入器、吸入器无效、嘴唇或手指发紫、对方筋疲力尽或意识混乱、呼吸变得安静或缓慢，或完成第一轮后症状仍未缓解。',
  'Severe bleeding': '严重出血',
  'Apply firm, continuous direct pressure over the wound with whatever is available — a cloth, clothing, your hand.': '用手边任何东西（布、衣物、您的手）在伤口上持续用力直接按压。',
  'Life-threatening limb bleeding not controlled by pressure: apply a tourniquet a few centimetres above the wound — never over a joint — and tighten until the bleeding stops. Note the exact time it went on and do not loosen it.': '按压无法控制的危及生命的肢体出血：在伤口上方几厘米处绑止血带，切勿绑在关节上，并拧紧直到出血停止。记下绑上的确切时间，且不要松开。',
  'A deep wound somewhere a tourniquet cannot go (neck, groin, armpit): pack the wound firmly and press.': '止血带无法使用的部位（颈部、腹股沟、腋窝）的深部伤口：把伤口紧紧填塞并按压。',
  'Call the emergency number for any severe bleeding.': '任何严重出血都要拨打紧急电话。',
  'A proper manufactured tourniquet is best; sources genuinely disagree on improvising one from a belt or scarf as a last resort — most say it is better than nothing for life-threatening limb bleeding, one major source (Mayo Clinic) advises against it. If a limb is bleeding life-threateningly and nothing manufactured exists, an improvised tourniquet — a firm, wide band tightened with a rigid object — is the safer choice for most authorities.': '专业制造的止血带最好；对于在万不得已时用腰带或围巾临时制作的做法，各来源确实存在分歧，大多数认为对危及生命的肢体出血总比什么都不做强，有一个主要来源（梅奥诊所）则建议不要这样做。如果肢体出血危及生命且没有专业产品，大多数权威机构认为临时止血带，即用硬物拧紧的宽而牢固的带子，是更安全的选择。',
  'Shock': '休克',
  'Signs: pale, cold, clammy skin, rapid weak pulse, rapid shallow breathing, confusion or weakness.': '表现：皮肤苍白、冰冷、湿黏，脉搏快而弱，呼吸快而浅，意识混乱或虚弱。',
  'Treat the visible cause (e.g. control any bleeding).': '处理可见的原因（例如控制任何出血）。',
  'Lie the person down; raise their legs if there is no injury (a leg fracture or suspected spinal injury) that raising them would make worse.': '让对方躺下；如果没有会因抬高双腿而加重的损伤（腿部骨折或疑似脊柱损伤），请抬高其双腿。',
  'Keep them warm, loosen tight clothing, give nothing to eat or drink.': '为其保暖，松开紧身衣物，不要给其吃喝任何东西。',
  'Call the emergency number.': '拨打紧急电话。',
  'Burns and scalds': '烧伤和烫伤',
  'Cool with cool (not ice-cold) running water for 20 minutes, starting as soon as possible — still worth doing up to about 3 hours after the burn.': '用凉的（不是冰冷的）流水冲洗 20 分钟，越早开始越好，即使在烧伤后约 3 小时内也仍值得这样做。',
  'Remove jewellery and clothing near the burn unless it is stuck to the skin.': '取下烧伤部位附近的首饰和衣物，除非它们粘在皮肤上。',
  'Cover loosely with cling film (not wrapped tightly around a limb) or a clean, non-fluffy dressing.': '用保鲜膜（不要紧紧缠绕肢体）或干净、不掉毛的敷料松松地覆盖。',
  'Chemical burn: flush continuously with plenty of water.': '化学烧伤：用大量清水持续冲洗。',
  'See a doctor for: a burn larger than the person’s palm; on the face, hands, feet, genitals or a major joint; any blistering burn in a baby or young child; or any electrical or chemical burn.': '出现以下情况请就医：烧伤面积大于患者手掌；位于面部、手、脚、生殖器或主要关节；婴幼儿任何起水疱的烧伤；或任何电烧伤或化学烧伤。',
  'No ice, butter, toothpaste, creams or oils.': '不要用冰、黄油、牙膏、药膏或油。',
  'Do not burst blisters.': '不要弄破水疱。',
  'Heat exhaustion and heat stroke': '热衰竭与中暑',
  'Heat stroke — confusion, agitation, drowsiness, collapse, hot skin that has STOPPED sweating, seizures: this is a medical emergency. Call for help and start cooling immediately.': '中暑：意识混乱、烦躁、嗜睡、昏倒、皮肤发烫且已停止出汗、抽搐，这是医疗急症。请呼救并立即开始降温。',
  'Whole-body cold-water immersion (up to the neck) is the fastest method if available. If not: pour or soak with cold water and fan the person, with ice packs at the neck, armpits and groin.': '如有条件，全身浸入冷水（至颈部）是最快的方法。否则：向对方浇冷水或用冷水浸湿，并扇风，同时在颈部、腋窝和腹股沟放置冰袋。',
  'Do not give anything to drink if the person is confused or not fully alert.': '如果对方意识混乱或不完全清醒，不要给其任何饮品。',
  'Heat exhaustion (milder — heavy sweating, tiredness, headache, nausea, still alert): move to shade, cool the skin, sip water or an oral rehydration/sports drink.': '热衰竭（较轻：大量出汗、疲倦、头痛、恶心，但仍清醒）：移到阴凉处，给皮肤降温，小口喝水或口服补液盐 / 运动饮料。',
  'Seizure (fit)': '癫痫发作（抽搐）',
  'Protect them from injury — move hazards away; do not move the person unless they are somewhere dangerous.': '保护其免受伤害：移开危险物品；除非对方处于危险的地方，否则不要移动对方。',
  'Cushion the head; do not restrain them; put nothing in the mouth.': '垫住头部；不要约束对方；不要往口中放任何东西。',
  'Time the seizure.': '给发作计时。',
  'Once the jerking stops, place them in the recovery position (above).': '抽搐停止后，让其采取复原卧位（见上文）。',
  'Call the emergency number if: it lasts longer than 5 minutes, it repeats, it is their first ever seizure, they are injured, in water, pregnant, diabetic, or not waking up afterwards.': '出现以下情况请拨打紧急电话：持续超过 5 分钟、反复发作、这是其第一次发作、对方受伤、在水中、怀孕、有糖尿病，或事后没有醒来。',
  'Febrile seizures in young children: same basic first aid — never put the child in a cold bath or undress them to bring a fever down.': '幼儿热性惊厥：基本急救相同，切勿把孩子放进冷水浴或脱光其衣服来降温。',
  'Head or neck injury, road crash': '头部或颈部受伤、车祸',
  'Do not move the person unless they are in immediate danger. Keep the head and neck as still as possible.': '除非对方处于直接危险中，否则不要移动。尽量保持头部和颈部不动。',
  'A motorcycle helmet: leave it on unless you need to remove it to clear the airway or because they are not breathing.': '摩托车头盔：除非需要摘下以打开气道或因对方没有呼吸，否则请保持戴着。',
  'Get to hospital for: repeated vomiting, increasing drowsiness or confusion, a worsening or persistent severe headache, a seizure, clear or blood-stained fluid from the nose or ears, or unequal pupil size.': '出现以下情况请去医院：反复呕吐、越来越嗜睡或意识混乱、加重或持续的剧烈头痛、抽搐、鼻或耳流出清亮或带血的液体，或瞳孔大小不等。',
  'Heart attack': '心脏病发作',
  'Call the emergency number — do not delay this to find aspirin or for any other reason.': '拨打紧急电话，不要为了找阿司匹林或任何其他原因而耽搁。',
  'Help the person sit down and rest in a comfortable position.': '帮助对方坐下，并以舒适的姿势休息。',
  'If they are not allergic to aspirin, have no bleeding disorder, and have not already taken a full dose: have them chew an aspirin while waiting for help (chew a dose in the 150–500 mg range — 300 mg is standard in the UK, 162–325 mg in the US).': '如果对方对阿司匹林不过敏、没有出血性疾病且尚未服过完整剂量：在等待救援时让其嚼服一片阿司匹林（嚼服 150–500 毫克范围内的一个剂量，英国标准为 300 毫克，美国为 162–325 毫克）。',
  'Stroke — FAST': '中风：FAST',
  'F — Face: has one side dropped?': 'F（面部）：是否有一侧下垂？',
  'A — Arms: can they raise both, or does one drift down?': 'A（手臂）：能否同时抬起双臂，还是有一侧下垂？',
  'S — Speech: is it slurred, or can they not speak?': 'S（言语）：是否含糊不清，或无法说话？',
  'T — Time: if any of these, call the emergency number immediately and note the exact time symptoms started — treatment is time-critical.': 'T（时间）：只要出现其中任何一项，请立即拨打紧急电话，并记下症状开始的确切时间，治疗对时间要求很高。',
  '(Some guidance uses "BE FAST", adding Balance and Eyes — a strokes affecting balance or vision can be missed by the classic FAST test alone.)': '（有些指南使用“BE FAST”，增加了平衡（Balance）和眼睛（Eyes），影响平衡或视力的中风，仅用经典的 FAST 测试可能被漏掉。）',
  'Give nothing by mouth — food, drink or medicine — until swallowing has been medically checked.': '在经医学检查确认吞咽功能之前，不要经口给予任何东西，包括食物、饮品或药物。',
  'Low blood sugar (hypoglycaemia)': '低血糖',
  'Conscious and able to swallow: give 15–20 g of fast-acting sugar — glucose tablets, a sugary (not diet) drink, or sweets.': '神志清醒且能吞咽：给予 15–20 克速效糖，如葡萄糖片、含糖（非无糖）饮料或糖果。',
  'Recheck after 10–15 minutes and repeat if still low; once recovered, follow with a slower-acting snack.': '10–15 分钟后再次检测，如仍偏低则重复；恢复后，再吃一些吸收较慢的零食。',
  'Drowsy, confused or unconscious: give nothing by mouth (choking risk), put them in the recovery position, and call the emergency number. Give glucagon if one is available and you are trained to use it.': '嗜睡、意识混乱或昏迷：不要经口给予任何东西（有窒息风险），让其采取复原卧位，并拨打紧急电话。如有胰高血糖素且您受过使用培训，请予以注射。',
  'When a child’s fever needs same-day care': '儿童发烧何时需要当天就医',
  'Under 3 months old with a temperature of 38°C (100.4°F) or higher: same-day medical assessment, even if the baby seems otherwise well.': '3 个月以下婴儿体温达到 38°C（100.4°F）或更高：当天做医疗评估，即使婴儿看起来其他方面良好。',
  '3–6 months old with a temperature of 39°C (102.2°F) or higher: get medical advice the same day.': '3–6 个月婴儿体温达到 39°C（102.2°F）或更高：当天寻求医疗建议。',
  'A child’s appearance and behaviour matter as much as the exact number — treat any of the red-flag signs below as urgent regardless of the reading on the thermometer.': '孩子的外观和行为与具体数字同样重要，无论体温计读数如何，出现下列任何危险信号都应视为紧急。',
  'Red flags in a baby or child — get emergency care now': '婴幼儿的危险信号：立即获取急救',
  'Does not respond normally, is very hard to wake, or is floppy.': '没有正常反应、很难叫醒或软绵绵。',
  'Blue, grey, very pale or blotchy skin or lips.': '皮肤或嘴唇发紫、发灰、非常苍白或有斑块。',
  'Struggling to breathe — grunting, sucking in around the ribs, or pauses in breathing.': '呼吸困难：发出呼噜声、肋骨周围凹陷，或呼吸暂停。',
  'A rash that does not fade when a glass is pressed against it.': '用玻璃杯按压后不褪色的皮疹。',
  'A fit or seizure.': '抽搐或癫痫发作。',
  'Signs of dehydration: sunken eyes, no tears, dry mouth, very few wet nappies, a sunken soft spot.': '脱水迹象：眼窝凹陷、没有眼泪、口干、湿尿布很少、囟门凹陷。',
  'A bulging soft spot (fontanelle), a stiff neck, or a high-pitched, weak or continuous cry.': '囟门隆起、颈部僵硬，或哭声尖锐、微弱或持续不停。',
  'Diarrhoea, vomiting & dehydration': '腹泻、呕吐与脱水',
  'Give oral rehydration solution (ORS) in small, frequent sips. Keep breastfeeding or feeding as normal.': '少量多次地给予口服补液盐（ORS）。继续母乳喂养或正常喂食。',
  'No ORS packet available: 6 level teaspoons of sugar and half a level teaspoon of salt, dissolved in 1 litre of clean water — measure the salt carefully, too much can be harmful.': '没有 ORS 包：6 平茶匙糖和半平茶匙盐，溶于 1 升干净的水中，请仔细量盐，过多可能有害。',
  'Zinc supplementation, where advised: 10 mg/day under 6 months, 20 mg/day over 6 months, for 10–14 days.': '如医嘱补锌：6 个月以下每天 10 毫克，6 个月以上每天 20 毫克，持续 10–14 天。',
  'Seek urgent care if the child cannot keep fluids down, passes little or no urine, or shows any of the red-flag signs above.': '如果孩子无法保持摄入液体、排尿很少或没有，或出现上述任何危险信号，请立即就医。',
  'Do not give anti-diarrhoea medicine such as loperamide to a child under 12 without a doctor’s advice, and never to a child who is unwell, dehydrated, or has bloody diarrhoea.': '未经医生建议，不要给 12 岁以下儿童服用洛哌丁胺等止泻药，对身体不适、脱水或有血性腹泻的儿童更不能使用。',
  'Giving a child paracetamol or ibuprofen': '给儿童服用对乙酰氨基酚或布洛芬',
  'Dose strictly by your child’s weight, following the pack or a doctor/pharmacist’s instructions.': '严格按孩子的体重给药，并遵循药品包装或医生 / 药剂师的说明。',
  'Do not give ibuprofen to a baby under 6 months, unless a doctor has said to (some guidance allows it from 3 months if the baby weighs at least 5 kg — check the product).': '6 个月以下婴儿不要服用布洛芬，除非医生说可以（有些指南允许体重至少 5 公斤的婴儿从 3 个月起使用，请查看产品说明）。',
  'Never give aspirin to anyone under 19 unless a doctor specifically prescribes it — the risk is Reye’s syndrome.': '除非医生明确开具，否则不要给 19 岁以下的任何人服用阿司匹林，风险是瑞氏综合征。',
  'If dengue is a possibility: paracetamol only — never ibuprofen or aspirin, because of bleeding risk.': '如果可能是登革热：只用对乙酰氨基酚，绝不能用布洛芬或阿司匹林，因为有出血风险。',
  'Dengue warning signs': '登革热警示症状',
  'Watch especially as a fever comes down (usually 24–48 hours after it breaks, around days 3–7 of illness) for: severe stomach pain, repeated vomiting (3 or more times in 24 hours), bleeding gums or nose, blood in vomit or stool, extreme tiredness, restlessness or irritability, rapid breathing, cold or clammy skin.': '退烧时（通常是退热后 24–48 小时，约在发病第 3–7 天）尤其要留意：剧烈胃痛、反复呕吐（24 小时内 3 次或以上）、牙龈或鼻出血、呕吐物或大便带血、极度疲倦、烦躁不安或易怒、呼吸急促、皮肤冰冷或湿黏。',
  'Any one of these means urgent medical care now.': '出现其中任何一项，都意味着需要立即就医。',
  'While waiting: paracetamol only, and keep the person drinking fluids.': '等待期间：只用对乙酰氨基酚，并让对方持续喝水。',
  'Babies and young children are at extra risk of severe dengue.': '婴幼儿患重症登革热的风险更高。',
  'A child swallows something poisonous': '孩子吞下了有毒的东西',
  'Do not make them vomit.': '不要催吐。',
  'Call the emergency number, or Thailand’s Ramathibodi Poison Center (1367, 24/7), and bring the container or packaging with you.': '拨打紧急电话，或泰国 Ramathibodi 中毒中心（1367，全天 24 小时），并带上容器或包装。',
  'A swallowed button battery is an emergency: go straight to hospital, do not wait.': '吞下纽扣电池属于紧急情况：直接去医院，不要等待。',
  'Over 1 year old, and the battery was swallowed within the last 12 hours, and the child can swallow normally: 10 mL (2 teaspoons) of honey by mouth every 10 minutes, up to 6 doses, on the way to hospital — this must never delay getting there.': '1 岁以上，且电池是在过去 12 小时内吞下、孩子能正常吞咽：在去医院途中，每 10 分钟口服蜂蜜 10 毫升（2 茶匙），最多 6 次，这绝不能耽误前往医院。',
  'Never give honey to a child under 1 year — botulism risk.': '1 岁以下儿童绝不能给蜂蜜，有肉毒杆菌中毒风险。',
  'Water safety for children': '儿童水上安全',
  'Constant, within-arm’s-reach supervision by one sober adult with no other task, whenever a child is in, on or near any water — pool, sea, river, even a bath.': '只要孩子在任何水域（泳池、海、河，甚至浴缸）中、水上或附近，就必须由一名清醒、没有其他事务的成人持续、在伸手可及的范围内看护。',
  'A properly fitted, approved child life jacket on boats or in open water.': '乘船或在开阔水域时，穿戴合身且经认证的儿童救生衣。',
  'Drowning is fast and silent, not splashy — it can happen in seconds with no cry for help.': '溺水又快又无声，不会水花四溅，几秒钟内就可能发生，且没有呼救声。',
  'Sun and heat with a baby': '婴儿的防晒与防热',
  'Keep babies under 6 months out of direct sun — shade, an umbrella or the stroller canopy, and light clothing are the main protection.': '6 个月以下婴儿应避免阳光直射：遮阴、使用伞或婴儿车遮篷，并穿轻薄衣物是主要的防护措施。',
  'If shade or clothing genuinely is not possible, a small amount of sunscreen on exposed skin such as the face is acceptable under 6 months.': '如果确实无法遮阴或穿衣，6 个月以下婴儿可在面部等裸露皮肤上少量涂抹防晒霜。',
  'Exclusively breastfed babies under 6 months do not need extra water, even in heat. Formula-fed babies may be given small amounts of cooled boiled water between feeds in hot weather.': '纯母乳喂养的 6 个月以下婴儿即使在炎热天气也不需要额外喝水。配方奶喂养的婴儿在炎热天气，两次喂奶之间可给少量放凉的开水。',
  'Watch for: fewer wet nappies, dark urine, dry mouth, no tears, unusual sleepiness or fussiness, hot/flushed skin — get medical help if these appear.': '请留意：湿尿布减少、尿色变深、口干、没有眼泪、异常嗜睡或烦躁、皮肤发热 / 潮红，如出现这些情况请就医。',
  'Mosquito repellent for babies and children': '婴幼儿驱蚊剂',
  'Under 2 months: no repellent at all — use a mosquito net over the cot or stroller, screened rooms and covering clothing instead.': '2 个月以下：完全不使用驱蚊剂，请改用婴儿床或婴儿车上的蚊帐、有纱窗的房间和遮盖皮肤的衣物。',
  'From 2 months: DEET up to 30% or picaridin are safe and effective (some countries, e.g. Canada, are more conservative and cap DEET at 10% for young children — check local guidance).': '从 2 个月起：浓度最高 30% 的 DEET 或派卡瑞丁是安全且有效的（有些国家如加拿大更为保守，对幼儿把 DEET 限制在 10%，请查看当地指南）。',
  'No oil of lemon eucalyptus (PMD) under 3 years.': '3 岁以下不要使用柠檬桉油（PMD）。',
  'Apply to your own hands first, then to the child’s face, avoiding eyes and mouth — or apply to clothing instead. Avoid the child’s hands.': '先涂在您自己的手上，再涂到孩子的脸上，避开眼睛和嘴巴，或改为涂在衣服上。避开孩子的手。',
  'Snake bite': '蛇咬伤',
  'Move away from the snake. Keep the person calm and lying as still as possible — movement and panic speed venom through the body.': '远离蛇。让伤者保持冷静并尽量平躺不动，活动和恐慌会加速毒液在体内扩散。',
  'Immobilise the bitten limb with a splint or sling. Remove rings, watches and tight clothing before swelling starts.': '用夹板或吊带固定被咬伤的肢体。在肿胀开始前取下戒指、手表和紧身衣物。',
  'Get to a hospital that can give antivenom as fast as possible.': '尽快前往能注射抗蛇毒血清的医院。',
  'If trained in it: a firm pressure bandage over the whole limb (pressure-immobilisation), plus the splint, is the preferred field technique in this region when the snake cannot be identified — but only if you know how, and never at the cost of delaying transport.': '如果受过相关培训：对整条肢体使用加压绷带（加压固定法），再加上夹板，是本地区在无法辨认蛇种时首选的现场方法，但前提是您懂得操作，且绝不能以延误转运为代价。',
  'Paracetamol, not aspirin or NSAIDs, if pain relief is needed — NSAIDs can worsen bleeding.': '如需止痛，请用对乙酰氨基酚，不要用阿司匹林或非甾体抗炎药，后者可能加重出血。',
  'Do not cut the wound or try to suck out venom.': '不要切开伤口，也不要试图把毒液吸出来。',
  'Do not apply a tight tourniquet, ice, an electric shock, alcohol or herbal remedies.': '不要使用紧扎的止血带，也不要冰敷、电击、涂酒精或使用草药偏方。',
  'Do not try to catch or kill the snake — a photo from a safe distance is fine, but never delay travel to identify it.': '不要试图抓蛇或打死蛇，在安全距离外拍张照片是可以的，但切勿为了辨认它而耽误送医。',
  'Washing the wound is fine and even sensible; do not scrub it or apply anything else to it.': '清洗伤口是可以的，甚至是明智的；不要擦洗，也不要在上面涂抹其他东西。',
  'Jellyfish sting (including box jellyfish)': '水母蜇伤（包括箱形水母）',
  'Get out of the water.': '离开水面。',
  'If not breathing normally: start CPR (above) — a box jellyfish sting can be life-threatening within minutes.': '如果呼吸不正常：开始心肺复苏（见上文），箱形水母蜇伤可在几分钟内危及生命。',
  'Pour plenty of vinegar on the sting for at least 30 seconds.': '在蜇伤处大量浇醋至少 30 秒。',
  'Then remove any remaining tentacles with tweezers, a card edge, or a gloved hand — protect yourself from being stung too.': '然后用镊子、卡片边缘或戴手套的手取下残留的触手，注意保护自己不被蜇到。',
  'Afterwards, for pain: either hot water or a cold pack may help — sources disagree on which is better, so use whichever is available.': '之后针对疼痛：热水或冷敷袋都可能有帮助，各来源对哪种更好有分歧，用手边有的即可。',
  'Call the emergency number for severe pain, breathing difficulty, chest discomfort, confusion or collapse. Worse within 30 minutes → urgent care regardless.': '如出现剧烈疼痛、呼吸困难、胸部不适、意识混乱或昏倒，请拨打紧急电话。30 分钟内加重则无论如何都要紧急就医。',
  'Do not rub the area.': '不要揉搓该部位。',
  'Do not rinse with fresh water — it can trigger more stings.': '不要用淡水冲洗，否则会引发更多刺细胞放毒。',
  'No alcohol, and no urine.': '不要使用酒精，也不要使用尿液。',
  'Stingray, stonefish or lionfish spine injury': '魟鱼、石鱼或狮子鱼的刺伤',
  'Immerse the wound in water as hot as can be comfortably tolerated without scalding (around 45°C) for roughly 20–90 minutes, or until the pain is controlled.': '把伤口浸泡在能舒适忍受、不至于烫伤的最热的水中（约 45°C），大约 20–90 分钟，或直到疼痛得到控制。',
  'Leave an embedded spine or barb in place — it may be plugging the wound — unless a medical professional tells you to remove it.': '嵌入的刺或倒钩请留在原处，它可能正堵着伤口，除非医务人员告诉您取出。',
  'Get medical care afterwards: infection risk, a possible retained fragment, antivenom (stonefish), and tetanus risk are all real.': '之后请就医：感染风险、可能残留的碎片、抗蛇毒血清（石鱼）和破伤风风险都是真实存在的。',
  'A sea urchin puncture is different — do NOT use the hot-water method. Wash it with soap and water instead, and seek care if a spine has gone into a joint.': '海胆刺伤则不同：不要使用热水浸泡法。请改用肥皂和水清洗，如果刺扎进了关节，请就医。',
  'Blue-ringed octopus or cone snail': '蓝环章鱼或芋螺',
  'Keep the person still and calm.': '让伤者保持不动并冷静。',
  'Apply a firm pressure-immobilisation bandage over the site and along the whole limb, then splint it — the same technique used for a dangerous snake bite.': '在伤处并沿整条肢体用加压固定绷带，然后上夹板，与处理危险毒蛇咬伤的方法相同。',
  'Call the emergency number and get to a hospital without waiting for symptoms to appear.': '拨打紧急电话并前往医院，不要等症状出现。',
  'Be ready to give rescue breaths or CPR — the venom can paralyse breathing for several hours, with no antivenom for either animal, and resuscitation must continue until professional help takes over.': '做好进行人工呼吸或心肺复苏的准备：毒液可能使呼吸麻痹数小时，这两种动物都没有抗毒血清，复苏必须持续到专业人员接手。',
  'Both animals are present in Thai waters (Gulf of Thailand and Andaman Sea); real encounters are rare, since both favour deeper water than most swimmers use, but the risk is severe enough to know this before it happens. Hot water does NOT help this sting (unlike a fish spine) — the toxin is heat-stable.': '这两种动物在泰国水域（泰国湾和安达曼海）都有；真正遇到的情况很少，因为它们都偏好比大多数游泳者所用水域更深的海水，但风险严重，值得在发生之前就了解。热水对这种蜇伤没有帮助（与鱼刺不同），毒素耐热。',
  'Animal bite, scratch or lick on broken skin (rabies risk)': '动物咬伤、抓伤或舔到破损皮肤（有狂犬病风险）',
  'Wash the wound thoroughly with soap and running water for at least 15 minutes (up to 20 minutes per Thailand-specific guidance) immediately.': '立即用肥皂和流动的水彻底冲洗伤口至少 15 分钟（按泰国的专门指南最多 20 分钟）。',
  'Apply an antiseptic (povidone-iodine or alcohol) if you have it.': '如有消毒剂（聚维酮碘或酒精），请涂抹。',
  'Get to a clinic or hospital THE SAME DAY for rabies post-exposure treatment — do not wait to see if the animal seems sick. Vaccine (and immunoglobulin, where indicated) is available at provincial and most district hospitals in Thailand.': '请当天前往诊所或医院接受狂犬病暴露后治疗，不要等着看动物是否生病。在泰国，省级和大多数县级医院都有疫苗（以及在需要时的免疫球蛋白）。',
  'Vaccinated before the trip: you still need booster doses after a real exposure — say so at the clinic; you will need fewer doses and no immunoglobulin.': '出行前已接种疫苗：真正暴露后仍需要加强针，请在诊所说明这一点；您需要的剂量更少，也不需要免疫球蛋白。',
  'Dogs, cats, monkeys and bats can all carry rabies across Thailand, Vietnam, Cambodia and Laos. A lick on broken skin is treated the same as a bite or scratch.': '在泰国、越南、柬埔寨和老挝，狗、猫、猴子和蝙蝠都可能携带狂犬病毒。舔到破损皮肤与咬伤或抓伤的处理方式相同。',
  'Caught in a rip current': '被卷入离岸流',
  'Do not try to swim straight back to shore against it — you will exhaust yourself.': '不要试图逆流直接游回岸边，那只会使您筋疲力尽。',
  'Stay calm, float or tread water, and raise an arm and call out to signal for help.': '保持冷静，漂浮或踩水，举起一只手臂并呼喊以求救。',
  'Swim parallel to the shore to escape the current, or let it carry you out until it weakens (usually just past the breaking waves) and then swim back at an angle.': '平行于海岸游动以脱离水流，或让水流带您出去，直到它减弱（通常刚过碎浪区），然后斜向游回。',
  'A red flag means do not swim. Thailand’s south-west monsoon (roughly May–October) brings rough seas and dangerous rip currents, especially on Andaman (west) coast beaches — ferries and speedboats, including those serving the Trat islands, are sometimes suspended in rough weather.': '红旗表示禁止游泳。泰国西南季风（大约 5 月至 10 月）会带来汹涌的海浪和危险的离岸流，尤其是在安达曼（西侧）海岸的海滩，渡轮和快艇（包括前往达叻诸岛的班次）在恶劣天气时有时会停运。',
  'Lightning': '雷电',
  'Hearing thunder or seeing lightning nearby: get indoors into a substantial building, or into a hard-topped (metal-roof) vehicle with the windows up.': '听到雷声或看到附近有闪电：请进入坚固的建筑物内，或进入有硬顶（金属车顶）且车窗已关闭的车辆中。',
  'Get out of the water and off the beach at once — do not shelter under a beach pavilion, umbrella or open-sided shelter.': '立即离开水面和海滩，不要在海滩凉亭、遮阳伞或四面敞开的遮蔽处躲避。',
  'Wait at least 30 minutes after the last thunderclap before going back outside.': '最后一声雷响后至少等待 30 分钟再外出。',
  'A lightning-strike victim carries no electrical charge — it is safe to touch them immediately and start CPR if they are not breathing.': '雷击受害者身上不带电，可以立即触碰，如果没有呼吸，请立即开始心肺复苏。',
  'Calling for help in Thailand — beyond the main number': '在泰国求助：主号码之外',
  '1669 (medical emergency/ambulance) is free from any phone, works nationwide 24 hours, and operators can usually handle basic English — say "English" as soon as the call connects. Response is markedly slower on islands and in rural areas than in Bangkok.': '1669（医疗急救 / 救护车）从任何手机拨打都免费，全国 24 小时可用，接线员通常能应对基本英语，接通后请立即说“English”。海岛和乡村地区的响应明显比曼谷慢。',
  '191 is police, 199 is fire — both free and 24 hours.': '191 是警察，199 是消防，均免费，24 小时可用。',
  '1155 is the Tourist Police: a free, 24-hour hotline specifically staffed for English-speaking travellers — a good parallel or backup call, though not a replacement for 1669 in a medical emergency.': '1155 是旅游警察：一条免费的 24 小时热线，专门配备了会说英语的人员，可作为并行或备用的求助电话，但在医疗急症时不能代替 1669。',
  '1367 is the Ramathibodi Poison Center’s 24/7 consultation hotline.': '1367 是 Ramathibodi 中毒中心的 24 小时咨询热线。',
  '1199 is the Marine Department’s 24-hour hotline for water incidents (boats, ferries, accidents at sea).': '1199 是海事局的 24 小时热线，处理水上事件（船只、渡轮、海上事故）。',
  'This is Thailand-specific detail underneath the country’s own main emergency number, which this app already shows at the top of the SOS and hospital screens for whichever country you are in.': '这是泰国专属的细节，位于该国自己的主要紧急电话之下，本应用已在“紧急求助”和医院页面顶部显示您所在国家的主要紧急电话。',
  'Insurance and getting evacuated': '保险与紧急后送',
  'Comprehensive travel insurance covering medical treatment AND emergency evacuation (including from remote islands) is not optional here — do not assume your home healthcare system covers this.': '涵盖医疗和紧急后送（包括从偏远海岛后送）的全面旅行保险在这里不是可选项，不要假定您本国的医疗体系会承担这些。',
  'Foreigners are charged for all medical treatment; there is no reciprocal free-healthcare arrangement.': '外国人所有医疗都要收费；没有互惠的免费医疗安排。',
  'Private hospitals — the fastest, highest-standard option — commonly want a deposit or a formal insurer "guarantee of payment" before non-emergency treatment. Even with insurance, you may be billed as self-pay until that guarantee arrives, which can take 24–72 hours or more.': '私立医院是最快、标准最高的选择，通常在非紧急治疗前要求预付押金或保险公司正式的“付款担保”。即使有保险，在担保到位之前（可能需要 24–72 小时甚至更久），您也可能被按自费计费。',
  'Call your insurer’s assistance line as early as possible — ideally before admission, not after.': '请尽早联系保险公司的援助热线，最好在入院之前，而不是之后。',
  'Malaria, dengue and Japanese encephalitis risk': '疟疾、登革热和乙型脑炎风险',
  'Malaria in Thailand is concentrated in remote, forested border areas (with Cambodia, Myanmar and Malaysia) — the tourist islands themselves are low or negligible risk, and routine antimalarial tablets are generally not needed for an island or beach trip.': '泰国的疟疾集中在偏远的森林边境地区（与柬埔寨、缅甸和马来西亚交界处），旅游海岛本身风险很低或可忽略，海岛或海滩之旅一般不需要常规服用抗疟药。',
  'Dengue is different: it is endemic across Thailand, Vietnam, Cambodia and Laos, including all the islands, year-round with a rainy-season peak. There is no vaccine relied on for casual travel — bite avoidance (repellent, covering clothing, screens) is the real prevention.': '登革热则不同：它在泰国、越南、柬埔寨和老挝（包括所有海岛）全年流行，雨季达到高峰。目前没有可供一般旅行依赖的疫苗，避免蚊虫叮咬（驱蚊剂、遮盖皮肤的衣物、纱窗）才是真正的预防办法。',
  'Japanese encephalitis occurs countrywide outside Bangkok, peaking seasonally (roughly May–October), and is weighted toward rural, rice-farming areas. Vaccination is mainly advised for longer stays (a month or more) or higher-risk itineraries.': '乙型脑炎在曼谷以外的全国范围内发生，有季节性高峰（大约 5 月至 10 月），多集中在乡村稻作地区。主要建议长期停留（一个月或以上）或风险较高的行程接种疫苗。',
  'Anyone trekking into remote forest near an international border should get individual pre-trip travel-clinic advice regardless of the above.': '无论上述情况如何，任何前往国际边境附近偏远森林徒步的人，都应在出发前向旅行门诊获取个人化的建议。',
};
